      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We can use the formula for finding the exponent of a prime $p$ in $n!$ which is given by:\n$$\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{p^k} \\right\\rfloor$$\nIn this case, we want to find the exponent of $3$ in $24!$, so we plug in $n=24$ and $p=3$ into the formula:\n$$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{3} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{3^2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{3^3} \\right\\rfloor + \\cdots$$\nCalculating each term, we get:\n$$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{3} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{9} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{27} \\right\\rfloor + \\cdots = 8 + 2 + 0 + \\cdots = \\boxed{10}$$\nSo the exponent of $3$ in $24!$ is $10$.The answer is: 10",
